DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Chicago Public Library\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mo
 nths\\nCategory: Storytime\\n\\nComic books are an internationally success
 ful form of storytelling thanks to movies\, TV shows\, and comic book conv
 entions. However\, not much is mentioned about the Black origins and contr
 ibutions in the comic book industry. Black people are responsible for some
  of the most popular and enduring characters ever known that have their ow
 n cult followings\, merchandise\, and even events like Blerdcon. The Black
  influence on comics is undeniable in making the comic book medium what it
  is today. The grou\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/ev
 ents/6a04bcba0c0f2c4503fa0307
